+4.  **Combine with Photometric Losses:** Integrate the perceptual loss into the total objective function. A standard formulation combines L1 and SSIM losses: $\mathcal{L} = (1 - \lambda_1 - \lambda_2)\mathcal{L}_1 + \lambda_1\mathcal{L}_{\text{SSIM}} + \lambda_2\mathcal{L}_{\text{PIPS}}$, where $\mathcal{L}_1$ is the L1 loss, $\mathcal{L}_{\text{SSIM}}$ is the structural similarity loss, and $\lambda_1, \lambda_2$ are weighting coefficients [S1]. To mitigate color shifts introduced by perceptual loss, an anti-bias term $\mathcal{L}_{ab}$ can be added, defined as the L1 distance between $k$-fold downsampled ground truth patch $P$ and predicted patch $\hat{P}$: $\mathcal{L}_{ab} = \| DSk(P) - DSk(\hat{P}) \|_1$ [S4]. The full objective becomes $\mathcal{L} = w_{l1} \mathcal{L}_{l1} + w_{vgg} \mathcal{L}_{vgg} + w_{ab} \mathcal{L}_{ab}$ [S4].
 5.  **Backpropagate:** Compute gradients with respect to the radiance field parameters using the combined loss and update the model [S4].
 
 **Parameters:**
-*   $\lambda_1, \lambda_2$ (or $w_{l1}, w_{vgg}, w_{ab}$): Weights for the respective loss terms. Values are not explicitly given in the primary sources [S1, S4].
+*   $\lambda_1, \lambda_2$ (or $w_{l1}, w_{vgg}, w_{ab}$): Weights for the respective loss terms. Values are not explicitly given in the sources [S1, S4].
